cff-version: 1.2.0

title: "BAAP: Bacterial Annotation & Analysis of Proteases"

version: "1.0.0"

type: software

message: "If you use BAAP in your research, please cite this software."

authors:
  - family-names: "Zindal"
    given-names: "Bisal"

abstract: >
  BAAP (Bacterial Annotation & Analysis of Proteases) is an open-source
  bioinformatics pipeline for genome-scale identification, annotation,
  classification, and validation of bacterial proteases. The pipeline
  integrates genome annotation, MEROPS-based similarity screening,
  InterProScan/Pfam domain evidence, protease classification, evidence
  evaluation, and structured reporting to distinguish supported proteases
  from putative, inactive, non-protease, and review candidates.

keywords:
  - bacterial proteases
  - protease annotation
  - protease classification
  - bacterial genome
  - bioinformatics
  - MEROPS
  - InterProScan
  - Pfam
  - Prokka
  - protein annotation
  - computational biology
  - genome annotation
  - peptidases

license: "MIT"

